0	133	Peter Benjamin Mandelson, Baron Mandelson (born 21 October 1953), is a British former Labour Party politician, lobbyist and diplomat.
134	204	He was the Member of Parliament (MP) for Hartlepool from 1992 to 2004.
205	377	He served in Tony Blair and Gordon Brown's cabinets as Minister without portfolio, Secretary of State for Northern Ireland, Business Secretary and First Secretary of State.
378	472	He was the British Ambassador to the United States in 2025 under Prime Minister Keir Starmer.

472	575	Mandelson served as director of communications from 1985 to 1990 during the leadership of Neil Kinnock.
576	678	Sidelined during John Smith's leadership from 1992 to 1994, Mandelson became close to Blair and Brown.
679	834	He was widely regarded as one of the architects of New Labour and a key adviser to Blair, contributing to the party's election victories in 1997 and 2001.

834	1168	Mandelson served as Minister without Portfolio from 1997 to 1998, Secretary of State for Business, Innovation and Skills and President of the Board of Trade in 1998 and again from 2008 to 2010, Secret
1169	1339	He was European Commissioner for Trade from 2004 to 2008, being elevated to the House of Lords as a life peer in 2008 to serve in the Brown cabinet as business secretary.
1340	1439	After Labour lost the 2010 general election, Mandelson co-founded the lobbying firm Global Counsel.
1440	1571	He remained active in Labour politics, and was an adviser to Starmer before Labour's return to office at the 2024 general election.
1572	1760	During his tenure as ambassador to the United States, Mandelson focused on promoting trade and fostering relationships with the US government during the second presidency of Donald Trump.

1760	1908	Mandelson's career has been marked by controversy, which resulted in his twice resigning from the Cabinet and being dismissed as ambassador in 2025.
1909	2101	He bought a home in 1996 partly with an interest-free loan of £373,000 from Geoffrey Robinson, a Cabinet colleague whose business dealings were subject to an inquiry by Mandelson's department.
2102	2199	He had not declared the loan in the Register of Members' Interests and resigned in December 1998.
2200	2353	In January 2001 he again resigned from the government following accusations of using his position to influence a passport application for S. P. Hinduja.

2353	2524	In September 2025, a scandal arose concerning Mandelson's association with the financier and convicted child sex offender Jeffrey Epstein, which had been reported in 2019.
2525	2666	Following reports that Mandelson had continued the friendship following Epstein's 2008 conviction, he was dismissed as ambassador by Starmer.
2667	2867	In February 2026, further reports alleged that Mandelson and his husband had received payments from Epstein, and that in 2009 and 2010 Mandelson had passed sensitive government information to Epstein.
2868	3024	Mandelson subsequently resigned from the Labour Party and from the House of Lords, and the Metropolitan Police opened an investigation into the allegations.
3025	3145	He was later arrested on suspicion of misconduct in public office, then released on bail pending further investigation.

3145	3394	In April 2026, it was reported that UKSV had recommended against granting Mandelson security clearance in January 2025, but that officials in the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office overruled
3395	3558	A government spokesperson claimed the decision was taken by FCDO officials, and that Prime Minister Keir Starmer was not aware of the override until April 2026.



3558	3738	Early life and education
Peter Benjamin Mandelson was born on 21 October 1953, in Hendon, Middlesex, the younger son of George Norman ("Tony") Mandelson (1920–1988) and Mary Joyce.
3739	3870	His father George was advertising manager of The Jewish Chronicle and an officer in the Royal Dragoons during the Second World War.
3871	3958	His mother Mary was the daughter of Herbert Morrison and his first wife, Margaret Kent.
3959	4052	Morrison was a London County Council leader and a cabinet minister in the Attlee government.

4052	4150	Of Polish Jewish ancestry, his grandfather, Norman Mandelson, founded the Harrow United Synagogue.
4151	4311	Mandelson was raised in Hampstead Garden Suburb; recalling his childhood, he said "my whole upbringing was framed around the Suburb – my friendships and values.
4311	4409	"
Mandelson attended the Garden Suburb School, and from 1965 to 1972 Hendon County Grammar School.
